{ ============================================================
  ADAPTIVE FARMER - TREND LONG STRATEGY
  Signal Name : Strategy_TXF_60M_Breakout_B_ATR_V2_3_CPU_Opt
  MC Load Name: WILLY_ATR_LONG_60M
  Version     : V2.7 + StopProfit + FrozenSL + HolidayFlat_v3 + ImmediateStop
  Symbol      : TXF1 (Taiwan Stock Index Futures Front Month)
  Platform    : MultiCharts 9.0 PowerLanguage x64
  Timeframe   : Data1 = 45M / Data2 = Daily / Data3 = Weekly
                (NOTE: strategy name says 60M but Excel report
                 confirms compression = 45 Minutes. Name kept for
                 live continuity; actual chart is 45M.)

  CHANGELOG:
    V2.3  Label unification (TL_ prefix). No logic changes.
    V2.4  (2026-06-12) P5 Holiday module rebuilt as HolidayFlat_v3:
          - Iron Rule: flat (0 position) BEFORE the 05:00 close of
            the last night session preceding every market closure.
          - Old design (eve date >= 13:30) replaced: it missed the
            post-midnight tail (00:00-05:00 bars stamped with the
            next calendar date) and never blocked entries.
          - Array semantics changed: Holiday_Tail = last trading
            day + 1 calendar day (the tail-bar date stamp).
          - Date errors fixed: Labor Day added for every year;
            all three 2026 entries corrected vs official TAIFEX
            115-yr calendar; H2 2026 + 2027/1/1 added.
          - Header performance figures reflect the OLD module;
            re-backtest pending after deployment.
          - Fail-safe horizon guard: Registry_Valid_Until input.
            Beyond the last verified registry date the strategy
            blocks entries and flattens (TL_RegistryEnd) - future
            holidays beyond the published TAIFEX calendar are
            unknowable, so walking off the verified map must fail
            safe, not fail silent. 30-day red warning on chart.
    V2.5  (2026-06-12) P3 initial stop FROZEN at entry:
          - Old code recomputed the stop EVERY BAR from current
            45M ATR and Daily ATR, so the floor drifted with
            volatility during the trade (user observed the live
            stop shifting between reloads). Now computed once on
            the entry bar close and locked (v_SL_Locked pattern,
            same as L2 SL_Locked / S1 v_EntryATR).
          - MA55 trail (P4) still updates by design; the frozen
            initial stop is the floor it can never drop below.
          - No new inputs. No entry-logic change.
          - DEPLOYMENT: changes historical exits -> recalculated
            chart may disagree with a live open position. Deploy
            ONLY WHEN FLAT (see annotated doc deployment note).
    V2.6  (2026-06-12) P7 Stop Profit Guard, ported from L2
          (Trendbearish_V1 SECTION 12), user-directed:
          - Activation: CLOSE-based profit >= 250 pts. Peak profit
            (posbleProfit_Long) ratchets up only; lock floor =
            Entry + peak x 45 pct moves only in the profit
            direction and never disarms until flat.
          - Guarantees: an armed runner can never round-trip into
            a loss (floor > entry by construction); giveback from
            peak is capped at 55 pct.
          - Data basis (469-trade MFE audit): 83 trades reached
            +100pts yet closed negative (-1,520,200); MFE>=250
            trades gave back median 50 pct / P90 112 pct; Top-10
            endpoint giveback max only 28 pct -> 55 pct tolerance
            clears the fat tail with huge margin.
          - Integrated as a third floor in Final_Exit (single-stop
            architecture kept; L2 uses an order-priority chain
            instead - effect identical). New exit label TL_SP.
          - Optimistic-bound improvement +1.93M; path-level
            whipsaw cost invisible to MFE data -> MC9 A/B is the
            final arbiter. Deploy only when flat.
    V2.7  (2026-07-02) Plan A: SP threshold 250 -> 500.
          - Backtest (SP500 only): Net +3,938K (+22.5%), PF 1.484,
            MDD -461K, trades 451, win/loss 3.19x, avg +6001/trade.
          - TL_SP exits 68 -> 12; freed trades flow to TL_TP
            (103 -> 141), letting trends run longer.
          Plan C REJECTED after A/B test:
          - Re-entry after passive exit (TL_SL/TL_SP/TL_SL_Gap).
          - Hypothesis +2.1M looked attractive but MC9 path-level
            backtest (A+C combined, SP500) showed Net 3,018K vs
            Plan A alone 3,938K = -920K drag. 69 re-entry trades
            net negative. Re-entry positions hit SL at worse prices
            than original breakout entries.
          - Decision: Plan A only. Plan C code removed.
          - Deploy only when flat.
    V2.6+ (2026-06-18) P3b Immediate Stop Guard:
          - SetStopLoss = MC engine-level stop, active on the
            ENTRY BAR itself (no IOG dependency). Closes the
            structural 45-minute unprotected window between fill
            and first custom stop order (IOG=false -> script
            evaluates at bar close only).
          - Distance = same as P3 frozen SL: MaxList(ATR x 1.5,
            Daily_ATR x 0.5) x BigPointValue.
          - Called only when flat (MP<=0) -> freezes automatically
            when position established (same principle as V2.5
            Frozen SL via v_SL_Locked).
          - Does NOT replace P3/P4/P7 exit logic. Once custom
            stops tighten beyond SetStopLoss, engine picks the
            tighter level. SetStopLoss becomes dormant backup.
          - Deploy only when flat.

  STRATEGY LOGIC:
    P2 Entry  : Close crosses above MA61 + ATR x Entry_Multiplier
    P3 Stop   : Frozen at entry - MaxList(ATR x SL_Mult,
                Daily_ATR x Cap_Mult), locked for the whole trade
    P3b Guard : SetStopLoss (engine-level, active on entry bar)
                Covers the 45min IOG=false gap between fill and
                first custom stop order. Same distance as P3.
    P4 Trail  : MA55 - TrailOffset (breathing trail, let trend run)
    P7 Guard  : Stop Profit - armed at +500 pts close-based, lock
                floor = Entry + peak x 45 pct, ratchets up only
    P5 v3     : Pre-holiday flat rule (block entries on tail bars,
                forced market exit from Holiday_Flat_Time)
    P6 Filter : Data3 Weekly OR filter (20MA / 60MA)
    Exit      : single stop at Max(P4 trail, P3 frozen, P7 lock)

  PERFORMANCE (Excel Report 2026/07/02, SP 500, Initial Capital 1M):
    Net Profit    : 3,018,400 TWD
    Profit Factor : 1.496
    Win Rate      : 31.3%
    Win/Loss Ratio: 3.28x
    MDD           : -547,800 (-21.2%)
    Total Trades  : 476
    Avg Trade     : +6,341 TWD
    Backtest      : 2019/12/16 - 2026/07/02
  ============================================================ }

[IntrabarOrderGeneration = false]

Inputs:
    { P2: Attack Engine (Data1) }
    Length60(61),
    Entry_Multiplier(2.0),

    { P3: Defense Engine (Strict Stop-Loss) }
    SL_Multiplier(1.5),
    Daily_Cap_Multiplier(0.5),

    { P4: Trailing Engine (Legacy MA55) }
    Length20(55),
    TrailOffset(50),

    { P7: Stop Profit Guard (ported from L2 Trendbearish_V1) }
    stopProfitPoints_Long(500),    { activation: close-based profit >= this many points (V2.7: 250->500) }
    profitReturnPrcnt_Long(55),    { allowed giveback pct of peak profit }

    ATR_Length(20),

    { P5 v3: Pre-Holiday Flat Rule }
    Manual_Kill_Switch(False),
    Holiday_Flat_Time(345),        { 03:45 trigger -> fill 03:45, retry 04:30, flat before 05:00 close }
    Registry_Valid_Until(1270101), { last date covered by the verified holiday registry;
                                     beyond it the strategy fails safe: no entries, flatten all.
                                     Bump this when rebuilding the registry from the next
                                     TAIFEX annual calendar (Q4 each year). }

    { P6 (2026-06-17): Monthly Settlement Flat
      TXF1 settles every month's 3rd Wednesday at 13:30.
      Position held to settlement gets force cash-settled by exchange.
      Detection: DayOfWeek = 3 (Wed) AND DayOfMonth in [15,21].
      Flat-time 12:30 gives 1hr buffer before 13:30 settlement.
      Same exit-priority framework as Holiday_Flat_Time. }
    Settlement_Flat_Time(1230),    { 12:30 trigger before 13:30 monthly settlement }

    { P6: Data3 (Weekly) Filter Settings }
    Weekly_MA_Fast(20),
    Weekly_MA_Slow(60);

Variables:
    maBase(0),
    maTrail(0),
    Breakout_Level(0),
    Current_ATR(0),
    Daily_ATR(0),
    Cond_Breakout(False),
    MP(0),
    Entry_P(0),
    Exit_Price_ATR(0),
    Exit_Price_Cap(0),
    Exit_Price_SL(0),
    Exit_Price_Trail(0),
    Final_Exit_Price(0),
    v_SL_Locked(False),
    v_Frozen_SL(0),
    posbleProfit_Long(0),
    stopProfitPrice_L(0),

    { P5 v3 Module Variables }
    Init_Done(False),
    v_Holiday_Block(False),
    v_Registry_Expired(False),
    Registry_Warn_ID(-1),
    idx(0),

    { P6 Settlement Variables }
    v_Settlement_Day(False),

    { MDD Visual Tracking Variables }
    MyEquity(0),
    Current_Year_Log(0),
    Year_Start_Equity(0),
    Year_High_Equity(0),
    Year_DD(0),
    Year_Max_DD(0),
    Year_Net_Profit(0),
    txtID(0),
    strMsg(""),

    { P6: Weekly Filter Variables }
    v_Weekly_MA_Fast(0),
    v_Weekly_MA_Slow(0),
    v_Weekly_Filter(false);

Array:
    Holiday_Tail[80](0);

{ ==========================================
  0. P5 v3: Holiday Tail Registry (2019-2026)

  Holiday_Tail = the calendar date stamped on the 00:00-05:00
  tail bars of the LAST night session before each market
  closure. Always = last trading day + 1 calendar day
  (robust to closure length; Saturday tails are valid).

  Iron Rule: position must be 0 before that session's 05:00
  close. Tail bars block entries and force a market exit.

  Sources: TAIFEX official annual market calendars.
  - 2026 verified against the official 115-yr PDF (2026-06-12).
  - Entries marked * were MISSING from the old eve-based list
    (Labor Day every year; 2025 new statutory holidays) and are
    reconstructed; verify vs archived TAIFEX PDFs before
    trusting re-backtest stats on those windows.
  ========================================== }

if Init_Done = False then begin

    { --- 2019 --- }
    Holiday_Tail[1]  = 1190913;
    Holiday_Tail[2]  = 1191010;
    Holiday_Tail[3]  = 1200101;  { 2020 New Year }

    { --- 2020 --- }
    Holiday_Tail[4]  = 1200121;  { CNY }
    Holiday_Tail[5]  = 1200228;  { 228 }
    Holiday_Tail[6]  = 1200402;  { Tomb Sweeping }
    Holiday_Tail[7]  = 1200501;  { * Labor Day }
    Holiday_Tail[8]  = 1200625;  { Dragon Boat }
    Holiday_Tail[9]  = 1201001;  { Mid-Autumn }
    Holiday_Tail[10] = 1201009;  { National Day }
    Holiday_Tail[11] = 1210101;  { 2021 New Year }

    { --- 2021 --- }
    Holiday_Tail[12] = 1210206;  { CNY }
    Holiday_Tail[13] = 1210227;  { 228 }
    Holiday_Tail[14] = 1210402;  { Tomb Sweeping }
    Holiday_Tail[15] = 1210612;  { Dragon Boat }
    Holiday_Tail[16] = 1210918;  { Mid-Autumn }
    Holiday_Tail[17] = 1211009;  { National Day }
    Holiday_Tail[18] = 1211231;  { 2022 New Year }

    { --- 2022 --- }
    Holiday_Tail[19] = 1220127;  { CNY }
    Holiday_Tail[20] = 1220226;  { 228 }
    Holiday_Tail[21] = 1220402;  { Tomb Sweeping }
    Holiday_Tail[22] = 1220430;  { * Labor Day (5/2 make-up) }
    Holiday_Tail[23] = 1220603;  { Dragon Boat }
    Holiday_Tail[24] = 1220909;  { Mid-Autumn }
    Holiday_Tail[25] = 1221008;  { National Day }
    Holiday_Tail[26] = 1221231;  { 2023 New Year }

    { --- 2023 --- }
    Holiday_Tail[27] = 1230118;  { CNY }
    Holiday_Tail[28] = 1230225;  { 228 }
    Holiday_Tail[29] = 1230401;  { Tomb Sweeping }
    Holiday_Tail[30] = 1230429;  { * Labor Day }
    Holiday_Tail[31] = 1230622;  { Dragon Boat }
    Holiday_Tail[32] = 1230929;  { Mid-Autumn }
    Holiday_Tail[33] = 1231007;  { National Day }
    Holiday_Tail[34] = 1231230;  { 2024 New Year }

    { --- 2024 --- }
    Holiday_Tail[35] = 1240206;  { CNY }
    Holiday_Tail[36] = 1240228;  { 228 }
    Holiday_Tail[37] = 1240404;  { Tomb Sweeping }
    Holiday_Tail[38] = 1240501;  { * Labor Day }
    Holiday_Tail[39] = 1240608;  { Dragon Boat }
    Holiday_Tail[40] = 1240917;  { Mid-Autumn }
    Holiday_Tail[41] = 1241010;  { National Day }
    Holiday_Tail[42] = 1250101;  { 2025 New Year }

    { --- 2025 (* rows pending check vs 114-yr TAIFEX PDF) --- }
    Holiday_Tail[43] = 1250123;  { CNY }
    Holiday_Tail[44] = 1250228;  { 228 }
    Holiday_Tail[45] = 1250403;  { Tomb Sweeping }
    Holiday_Tail[46] = 1250501;  { * Labor Day }
    Holiday_Tail[47] = 1250530;  { Dragon Boat (5/30 make-up; old list had 1250530 as eve = the holiday itself, could never fire) }
    Holiday_Tail[48] = 1250927;  { * Teachers Day (9/29 make-up) }
    Holiday_Tail[49] = 1251004;  { Mid-Autumn }
    Holiday_Tail[50] = 1251010;  { * National Day }
    Holiday_Tail[51] = 1251024;  { * Retrocession Day (10/24 make-up) }
    Holiday_Tail[52] = 1251225;  { * Constitution Day }
    Holiday_Tail[53] = 1260101;  { 2026 New Year }

    { --- 2026 (verified: TAIFEX official 115-yr calendar) --- }
    Holiday_Tail[54] = 1260212;  { CNY: final trading day 2/11; 2/12-2/13 closed }
    Holiday_Tail[55] = 1260227;  { 228: 2/27 make-up, eve 2/26 }
    Holiday_Tail[56] = 1260403;  { Children/Tomb 4/3-4/6, eve 4/2 }
    Holiday_Tail[57] = 1260501;  { Labor Day 5/1-5/3, eve 4/30 }
    Holiday_Tail[58] = 1260619;  { Dragon Boat 6/19-6/21, eve 6/18 }
    Holiday_Tail[59] = 1260925;  { Mid-Autumn + Teachers 9/25-9/28, eve 9/24 }
    Holiday_Tail[60] = 1261009;  { National Day 10/9-10/11, eve 10/8 }
    Holiday_Tail[61] = 1261024;  { Retrocession 10/24-10/26, eve 10/23 (Saturday tail) }
    Holiday_Tail[62] = 1261225;  { Constitution 12/25-12/27, eve 12/24 }
    Holiday_Tail[63] = 1270101;  { 2027 New Year 1/1-1/3, eve 12/31 }

    { 2027 CNY onward: rebuild from TAIFEX 116-yr calendar in Q4 2026 }

    Init_Done = True;

end;

{ ==========================================
  1. Core Indicators Calculation
  ========================================== }

maBase  = Average(Close, Length60);
maTrail = Average(Close, Length20);

Current_ATR = AvgTrueRange(ATR_Length) of Data1;
Daily_ATR   = AvgTrueRange(ATR_Length) of Data2;

Breakout_Level = maBase + (Current_ATR * Entry_Multiplier);

{ ==========================================
  P6: Weekly Filter Logic (Data3 - Weekly)
  OR logic: either MA condition allows long entries.
  Trend strategies need early entry at trend inception.
  AND logic would miss the early bull phase.
  ========================================== }

v_Weekly_MA_Fast = Average(Close, Weekly_MA_Fast) of Data3;
v_Weekly_MA_Slow = Average(Close, Weekly_MA_Slow) of Data3;

if (Close of Data3 > v_Weekly_MA_Fast) or
   (Close of Data3 > v_Weekly_MA_Slow) then
    v_Weekly_Filter = true
else
    v_Weekly_Filter = false;

{ ==========================================
  1b. P5 v3: Holiday Tail Detection
  Tail bars only exist in the 00:00-05:00 window
  (Time <= 0500 guard keeps the scan cheap).
  Computed BEFORE entry logic so the gate uses
  the current bar's state, not the prior bar's.
  ========================================== }

v_Holiday_Block = False;

if Time <= 500 then begin
    for idx = 1 to 80 begin
        if Date = Holiday_Tail[idx] then
            v_Holiday_Block = True;
    end;
end;

{ Fail-safe: beyond the verified registry horizon the future
  holiday schedule is UNKNOWN (next TAIFEX annual calendar not
  yet published / not yet loaded). Never trade unverified dates:
  block all entries and flatten any position. }

v_Registry_Expired = False;

if Date > Registry_Valid_Until then begin
    v_Registry_Expired = True;
    v_Holiday_Block    = True;
end;

{ ==========================================
  P6 Settlement-Day Detection (2026-06-17 added)
  TXF1 monthly settlement = 3rd Wednesday of each month.
  Logic: DayOfWeek=3 (Wed in MC) AND DayOfMonth in [15,21].
  Dynamic detection - no registry needed (TAIFEX rule is stable).
  ========================================== }

v_Settlement_Day = (DayOfWeek(Date) = 3) and
                   (DayOfMonth(Date) >= 15) and
                   (DayOfMonth(Date) <= 21);

{ Live-chart warning: registry horizon within ~30 days }

if LastBarOnChart and
   DateToJulian(Date) >= DateToJulian(Registry_Valid_Until) - 30 then begin
    if Registry_Warn_ID < 0 then begin
        Registry_Warn_ID = Text_New(Date, Time, High + 400,
            "P5 HOLIDAY REGISTRY EXPIRES " +
            NumToStr(Registry_Valid_Until, 0) +
            " - REBUILD FROM TAIFEX CALENDAR");
        Text_SetColor(Registry_Warn_ID, Red);
        Text_SetSize(Registry_Warn_ID, 14);
        Text_SetAttribute(Registry_Warn_ID, 1, true);
    end;
end;

{ ==========================================
  2. Entry Logic (gated by Holiday Tail)
  ========================================== }

Cond_Breakout = (Close Crosses Over Breakout_Level);
MP = MarketPosition;

{ P3b: Immediate Stop Guard -- entry-bar protection (2026-06-18)
  SetStopLoss is MC engine-level: active on entry bar, no IOG dependency.
  Only called when flat -> freezes at signal-bar ATR once position opens. }
if MP <= 0 then
    SetStopLoss(MaxList(Current_ATR * SL_Multiplier,
                        Daily_ATR * Daily_Cap_Multiplier) * BigPointValue);

if MP = 0 and
   Cond_Breakout and
   (v_Weekly_Filter = true) and
   (v_Holiday_Block = false) and
   (v_Settlement_Day = false) then begin
    Buy ("TL_Entry") next bar at Market;
end;

{ ==========================================
  3. Exit Management (P3 and P4 Integrated)
  ========================================== }

if MP > 0 then begin

    Entry_P = EntryPrice;

    { P3 V2.5: Double-Layered Initial Stop, FROZEN at entry.
      Computed ONCE on the entry bar close and locked for the
      whole trade. The old per-bar recalculation let the floor
      drift with ATR during the holding period. }
    if v_SL_Locked = False then begin
        Exit_Price_ATR = Entry_P - (Current_ATR * SL_Multiplier);
        Exit_Price_Cap = Entry_P - (Daily_ATR   * Daily_Cap_Multiplier);
        v_Frozen_SL    = MaxList(Exit_Price_ATR, Exit_Price_Cap);
        v_SL_Locked    = True;
    end;

    Exit_Price_SL = v_Frozen_SL;

    { P7 V2.6: Stop Profit Guard (L2 SECTION 12 ported to long).
      Close-based peak profit ratchets up only; once armed the
      lock floor never disarms until flat. An armed runner can
      never round-trip into a loss. }
    if (Close - Entry_P) >= stopProfitPoints_Long then begin
        if (Close - Entry_P) > posbleProfit_Long then
            posbleProfit_Long = Close - Entry_P;
        stopProfitPrice_L = Entry_P +
            (posbleProfit_Long * (1.0 - profitReturnPrcnt_Long / 100.0));
    end;

    { P4: MA55 trail keeps updating BY DESIGN (let profits run).
      Final stop = highest of three components. The frozen SL and
      the SP lock never loosen; the trail component breathes both
      ways, so the effective stop may sag - but only within the
      band ABOVE the two locked floors, never below them. }
    Exit_Price_Trail = maTrail - TrailOffset;
    Final_Exit_Price = MaxList(Exit_Price_Trail,
                       MaxList(Exit_Price_SL, stopProfitPrice_L));

    { Execution with unified TL_ labels }
    if Close < Final_Exit_Price then begin
        Sell ("TL_SL_Gap") next bar at Market;
    end else begin
        if AbsValue(Final_Exit_Price - Exit_Price_SL) < 0.001 then
            Sell ("TL_SL") next bar at Final_Exit_Price Stop
        else if stopProfitPrice_L > 0 and
                AbsValue(Final_Exit_Price - stopProfitPrice_L) < 0.001 then
            Sell ("TL_SP") next bar at Final_Exit_Price Stop
        else
            Sell ("TL_TP") next bar at Final_Exit_Price Stop;
    end;

end else begin
    { Flat: release locks for the next trade }
    v_SL_Locked       = False;
    v_Frozen_SL       = 0;
    posbleProfit_Long = 0;
    stopProfitPrice_L = 0;
end;

{ ==========================================
  4. P5 v3: Pre-Holiday Forced Flat (Iron Rule)
  On tail bars, force a market exit from
  Holiday_Flat_Time (03:45) onward:
    45M grid -> trigger on the 03:45 bar, fill at
    03:45; retry on the 04:30 bar, fill at 04:30.
    Always flat before the 05:00 session close.
  Typhoon / unscheduled closures cannot be
  pre-coded: use Manual_Kill_Switch + the
  pre-holiday manual check (SOP sec 3-1).
  ========================================== }

if MP > 0 then begin

    if v_Registry_Expired then begin
        Sell ("TL_RegistryEnd") next bar at Market;
    end
    else if v_Holiday_Block and Time >= Holiday_Flat_Time then begin
        Sell ("TL_Holiday") next bar at Market;
    end
    else if v_Settlement_Day and Time >= Settlement_Flat_Time then begin
        Sell ("TL_Settlement") next bar at Market;
    end;

    if Manual_Kill_Switch = True then begin
        Sell ("TL_Kill") next bar at Market;
    end;

end;

{ ==========================================
  5. Annual MDD Visualizer Module
  No label changes needed in this section.
  ========================================== }

if CurrentBar = 1 then begin
    Current_Year_Log  = Year(Date);
    Year_Start_Equity = InitialCapital;
    Year_High_Equity  = InitialCapital;
    Year_Max_DD       = 0;
end;

MyEquity = InitialCapital + NetProfit + OpenPositionProfit;

if Year(Date) <> Current_Year_Log or LastBarOnChart then begin

    if LastBarOnChart and Year(Date) = Current_Year_Log then
        Year_Net_Profit = MyEquity - Year_Start_Equity
    else
        Year_Net_Profit = MyEquity[1] - Year_Start_Equity;

    if Current_Year_Log >= 2024 then begin
        strMsg = "Year: " + NumToStr(Current_Year_Log, 0) + NewLine +
                 "MDD: $" + NumToStr(Year_Max_DD, 0);
        if LastBarOnChart then
            txtID = Text_New(Date,    Time,    High    + 200, strMsg)
        else
            txtID = Text_New(Date[1], Time[1], High[1] + 200, strMsg);
        Text_SetStyle(txtID,     2, 1);
        Text_SetColor(txtID,     Green);
        Text_SetSize(txtID,      12);
        Text_SetAttribute(txtID, 1, true);
    end;

    Current_Year_Log = Year(Date);

    if LastBarOnChart = False then begin
        Year_Start_Equity = MyEquity[1];
        Year_High_Equity  = MyEquity[1];
        Year_Max_DD       = 0;
    end;

end;

if Year(Date) = Current_Year_Log then begin
    if MyEquity > Year_High_Equity then
        Year_High_Equity = MyEquity;
    Year_DD = Year_High_Equity - MyEquity;
    if Year_DD > Year_Max_DD then
        Year_Max_DD = Year_DD;
end;
